/**
 * Icon set for the explorer tree and builder option cards.
 *
 * Two surfaces, one source of truth:
 *   - `<FileIcon name="package.json" />`  — file-tree row glyphs
 *   - `<ProviderIcon group="auth" value="clerk" />` — option-card brand tiles
 *
 * One shape for every icon — an explicit React component that returns a
 * single `<svg>` taking `className` (no factory, no variants):
 *
 *     export function FooSvg({ className }: SvgProps) {
 *       return (
 *         <svg viewBox="…" className={className} aria-hidden="true">
 *           …paths…
 *         </svg>
 *       );
 *     }
 *
 * Provenance of the underlying artwork:
 *   - File-type and some brand glyphs (TypeScript, React, JSON, Prisma,
 *     Drizzle…) are extracted from the VSCode Material Icon Theme
 *     (MIT © Material Extensions). Full text: `apps/web/LICENSE-ICONS.md`.
 *   - Brand marks (Supabase, tRPC, Hono, Clerk, PostHog, Plausible, Resend,
 *     Langchain, better-auth, Bugsnag…) are the official upstream logos,
 *     cropped to the icon-only portion of the lockup when needed. Where the
 *     mark works in any tone we use `currentColor` so the tile adapts to the
 *     surrounding theme; otherwise the brand hex is kept verbatim.
 *   - Package-type glyphs (UI, utils, config, library) are CTS-internal
 *     concepts with no upstream brand, so they're wrapped Lucide icons —
 *     same shape, just a different source.
 *
 * No `<img>`, no network requests, no runtime resolution. Each icon keeps
 * its native viewBox so the path math stays correct at any render size.
 * Gradient `id`s are brand-prefixed (`hono-grad`, `plausible-grad-1`, …) so
 * two SVGs on the same page can't silently collide on a shared id.
 */

